From 0c61fbfcb49b4902dfe7afeb026f30db1be7953c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:09:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Standard memory of the host for the device configured by
 initialize

MFEM compiled with Umpire allocates the memory of the host with Umpire
as soon as a device is configured (HOST_UMPIRE), Umpire recording each
allocation in its map of allocations. The temporaries of the loops over
the elements made on the host (shape functions, element matrices) were
thus allocated and freed through this map: on the bubble of mm-opera-hpc
(467109 unknowns) on a GPU, the post-processings (stresses exported at
the nodes, L2 projection) took 59.8 s instead of 10.7 s, and the whole
computation 68 s instead of 14 s.

Before the configuration of the device, initialize sets the memory types
of MFEM: the standard memory of the host, and the default memory of the
device (DEVICE_UMPIRE if MFEM is compiled with Umpire, DEVICE
otherwise), or the standard memory of the host on both sides for a
configuration without GPU. The variable MFEM_MEMORY of MFEM still gives
them (MFEM_MEMORY=umpire restores the previous behaviour).

Tests: DeviceOptionTest-cpu (standard memory of the host),
DeviceOptionTest-cpu-umpire (MFEM_MEMORY=umpire, if MFEM is compiled
with Umpire), DeviceOptionTest-cuda (memories of the host and of the
device on the GPU).
